# Connected-Device tile + nRF52840-DK BLE→Grafana E2E (Tier-1)

Date: 2026-06-06
Board: nRF52840-DK (PCA10056, SN 1050258557) — native BLE, USB/J-Link
Build: build-nrf-dietemp  (plain app + -DCONFIG_BATTERY_TEMP_NTC=n -DCONFIG_BATTERY_TEMP_DIE=y)
Wire: v3 (no current sense on this board => base format; current/coulomb/SoH/RTE absent)
Gateway: run from iTerm, branch feat/grafana-connected-device

## Goals
1. First-ever full BLE -> gateway -> InfluxDB -> Grafana pipeline on the flagship nRF52840-DK
   (only NUCLEO had been E2E'd before).
2. Validate the new "Connected Device" Grafana tile (PR #30).

## Two bugs the live run exposed (invisible to unit tests + an isolated InfluxDB query)

1. Board name not distinguished. On macOS CoreBluetooth the advertised GAP name is
   often empty (the scanner matches by service UUID for this reason), so device.name
   was None and the InfluxDB `device` tag fell back to the static default "iBattery"
   for every board. FIX: read the GATT Device Name characteristic (0x2A00 =
   firmware CONFIG_BT_DEVICE_NAME) after connecting; prefer GATT name -> advertised
   name -> default (gateway resolve_device_tag, TDD).
2. Grafana tile showed "(no device)". The stat panel reduces NUMERIC fields by
   default, so the string `device` tag (field "Value") was ignored. Verified via
   Grafana /api/ds/query that the query DOES return the string. FIX: panel
   reduceOptions.fields = "/^Value$/" so the string is selected and rendered.

Also: the bare nRF defaulted to CONFIG_BATTERY_TEMP_NTC=y (external NTC on AIN1);
with no thermistor wired the floating ADC read ~107 C. Rebuilt with the on-die
sensor (TEMP_DIE) for a sane reading — no external hardware.

## BEFORE
  device tag = "iBattery" (same for every board); Temperature ~107 C (floating NTC);
  Connected Device tile = "(no device)".

## AFTER (serial)
  [v3 t=2019] V=3002 mV T=26.00 C SOC=100.00% PWR=1 ...
  [v3 t=8063] V=3000 mV T=25.75 C SOC=100.00% PWR=1 ...

## AFTER (gateway, iTerm)
  gateway.scanner: Found iBattery at C179F5A2-... (name='iBattery-nRF52840')
  Streaming from iBattery-nRF52840 (C179F5A2-...) -> InfluxDB

## AFTER (InfluxDB)
  schema.tagValues(device, -30m) => iBattery (stale), iBattery-nRF52840 (live)
  last voltage_v (-20s) => 3.005, device=iBattery-nRF52840
  last temperature_c    => 26.25, device=iBattery-nRF52840

## AFTER (Grafana)
  Connected Device tile = "iBattery-nRF52840"; Temperature = 26.3 C.
  (Gauges/trends briefly show BOTH device tags — the stale "iBattery" series ages
   out of the time window; this is the per-device breakout the `device` tag enables.)

## PASS
Full BLE pipeline proven on nRF52840-DK; Connected Device tile shows the real board
name; temperature realistic. Gateway tests 122 -> 126. RTE/SoH/current require the
INA219 (Tier-2), blocked on this DK's P0.26/P0.27 defect — not attempted.
